Best Laptop for Devs & CS Students — Compare & Decide
Day 48 of #60DaysOfClaudeAI 🚀
A single-file HTML app that ranks MacBook Air (M4) vs Dell XPS 13 vs ThinkPad X1 Carbon vs ASUS Zenbook 14 OLED for developers and CS students choosing a daily-driver laptop for coding, compiling, and multitasking.
Live Demo
Open laptop-compare-decide.html in any browser — zero dependencies, zero setup.
What it does
Ranks 4 laptops on Performance, RAM/Storage, Battery Life, and Build/Portability
Fixed, transparent weighting tuned for developer workloads (Performance 35%, RAM/Storage 25%, Battery 25%, Portability 15%)
Every data point is either a sourced fact or clearly flagged as an estimate
Built-in "How this was researched" panel — shows exactly where each number came from and how source conflicts were resolved
Full sources panel with 14 citations (Apple, Dell, ASUS, Notebookcheck, NanoReview, Consumer Reports, XDA Developers, and more)
Responsive, dark-mode UI with graceful loading/error states
Why it's different
Most spec-comparison content just copies vendor marketing claims. This app explicitly separates vendor claims from independent test results — and flags it every time they disagree (e.g. Apple claims 18h battery, Consumer Reports measured 15h; Lenovo claims up to 19h, real-world testing showed 5–8h).
Tech
Pure HTML/CSS/JavaScript — no frameworks, no CDNs, no build step
Single file, works offline, works anywhere
Built with
Claude Sonnet 5 — research, data verification, and full app generation in one conversation.
